stories.body:
@gpusteve posted that the latest round did not go according to plan. The team had aimed for $18 million and instead closed a $40 million Series A, co led by @MarathonMP and @chemistry.

The same founder had just warned that the @wafer_ai account was hacked, and Wafer was already selling GLM 5.3 Flash on OpenRouter under that name. Treat the company handle as contested until they recover it.

Watch the rest of the investor list, whether the $40 million is cash in the bank or a headline package, and whether Wafer keeps selling open weight traffic after the account scare.

@edwardjhu asked how you RL post train a 397B model for long horizon knowledge work, then posted the answer the team actually ran. They took Qwen 3.5 397B from 16.1 percent Pass@1 to 27.3 percent on APEX Agents with DPPO, and said they are sharing the final model weights and the full training script.

This is a recipe and a weight drop on a huge Qwen cook, not a new Alibaba pretrain. The map change is that a 397B agent stack is being documented end to end instead of locked in a lab note.

Watch whether the files match the claimed APEX Agents jump, and whether other hosts pick up the DPPO recipe on the same 397B base.

@alexwg posted that Physical Superintelligence PBC, which he co founded with @matthew_pines and @AKlokus, has raised a 58 million seed round to build a research lab for discovering and commercializing physics breakthroughs at scale. A follow up said Breakthrough led the round, with Valkyrie, SV Angel, 021t, Robot Ventures, Susa Ventures, Variant, Dragon Global, Solari Ventures, Thomas Wolf, Balaji Srinivasan, Anthony Scaramucci, Robert Leshner, Philip Johnston, and others in the round.

Pines said this century still runs on last century’s physics, and that AI can change that. They pointed strategic customers at compute, energy, propulsion, communication, sensing, and actuation, and said they are hiring physicists, AI researchers, and engineers in Cambridge, MA.

This is a seed for a lab, not a new model. Watch whether PSI actually stands up that lab, and whether the seed turns into a machine you can buy.
